WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.671
JAMIE: How is that a Wall Street
story and

00:00:02.671 --> 00:00:05.342
JAMIE: not just a startup tragedy
story?

00:00:05.427 --> 00:00:08.158
RUFUS: Because the question those
analysts are asking is:

00:00:08.158 --> 00:00:10.890
RUFUS: what does this tell us
about Meta's data

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:13.621
RUFUS: strategy? Sundial built
what they called "agentic
analysts"

00:00:13.621 --> 00:00:16.353
RUFUS: — AI agents that could
autonomously clean messy

00:00:16.353 --> 00:00:19.084
RUFUS: data and surface insights,
through tools like Slack.

00:00:19.084 --> 00:00:21.816
RUFUS: Picture a junior analyst
who never sleeps and

00:00:21.816 --> 00:00:24.547
RUFUS: doesn't complain about
spreadsheet formatting.

00:00:24.612 --> 00:00:26.065
ALEX: Back to the wider story.

00:00:26.175 --> 00:00:28.426
RUFUS: Meta just bought that
person and told everyone

00:00:28.426 --> 00:00:30.676
RUFUS: else they can't hire them
anymore.

00:00:30.889 --> 00:00:32.947
JAMIE: And Sundial had raised
twenty-three million dollars
before

00:00:32.947 --> 00:00:35.004
JAMIE: this.
